# Self-Review Command

Run Simplify agent and Scrutinize agent sequentially on changed files for post-implementation quality refinement.

## Usage

/self-review              (auto-detect changed files from git)
/self-review <file>...    (review specific files)

## Phases

### Phase 0: Context Gathering

<!-- learning:on -->
**Produces:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, DECISIONS_CONTEXT, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, HEAD_BEFORE
<!-- learning:off -->
**Produces:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, HEAD_BEFORE
<!-- learning:end -->

Detect changed files and build context:

1. If arguments provided, use those as FILES_CHANGED
2. Else run `git diff --name-only HEAD` + `git diff --name-only --cached` to get staged + unstaged
3. If no changes found, report "No changes to review" and exit
4. Build TASK_DESCRIPTION from recent commit messages or branch name
5. Record `HEAD_BEFORE` (`git rev-parse HEAD`) now, before Simplify runs — Phase 3 compares against it

{{settings.settings_resolve()}}

{{decisions_load()}}
<!-- learning:on -->
Pass `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` to Scrutinize agent — the compact index lists active ADR/PF entries; Scrutinize agent uses `devflow:apply-decisions` to Read full entry bodies on demand. Known pitfalls help identify reintroduced issues, prior decisions help validate architectural consistency. (Simplify agent does not consume decisions — it operates at code-shape level and Scrutinize agent runs after to catch any architectural drift.)

<!-- learning:end -->
{{knowledge_load()}}

Pass `FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE` to Scrutinize agent.

<!-- learning:on -->
**Extract:** FILES_CHANGED (list), TASK_DESCRIPTION (string), DECISIONS_CONTEXT (string, optional), FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE (string, optional), HEAD_BEFORE (40-hex SHA)
<!-- learning:off -->
**Extract:** FILES_CHANGED (list), TASK_DESCRIPTION (string), FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE (string, optional), HEAD_BEFORE (40-hex SHA)
<!-- learning:end -->

### Phase 1: Simplify agent (Code Refinement)

**Produces:** SIMPLIFY_COMMITS
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION

Spawn Simplify agent to refine code for clarity and consistency:

Agent(subagent_type="Simplify", run_in_background=false):
"TASK_DESCRIPTION: {task_description}
FILES_CHANGED: {files_changed}
Simplify and refine the code for clarity and consistency while preserving functionality.
Commit any improvements with a conventional-commit message."

**Wait for completion.** Simplify agent commits changes directly.

### Phase 2: Scrutinize agent (9-Pillar Quality Gate)

**Produces:** SCRUTINIZE_STATUS
<!-- learning:on -->
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, DECISIONS_CONTEXT
<!-- learning:off -->
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION
<!-- learning:end -->

Spawn Scrutinize agent for quality evaluation and fixing:

Agent(subagent_type="Scrutinize", run_in_background=false):
"TASK_DESCRIPTION: {task_description}
FILES_CHANGED: {files_changed}
<!-- learning:on -->
DECISIONS_CONTEXT: {decisions_context}
<!-- learning:end -->
FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE: {feature_knowledge}
Evaluate against 9-pillar framework. Fix P0/P1 issues. Return structured report.
<!-- learning:on -->
Follow devflow:apply-decisions to scan DECISIONS_CONTEXT and Read full ADR/PF bodies on demand. Skip if (none).
<!-- learning:end -->
Follow devflow:apply-feature-knowledge for FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE. Skip if (none)."

**Wait for completion.** Extract: STATUS (PASS|FIXED|BLOCKED) from the `### Status` line

### Phase 3: Conditional Validation

**Produces:** VALIDATION_RESULT
**Requires:** HEAD_BEFORE, SCRUTINIZE_STATUS

If STATUS is BLOCKED, skip this phase: the report (Phase 4) names the blocker.

Run this phase only if HEAD moved — `git rev-parse HEAD` differs from `HEAD_BEFORE`, meaning Simplify or Scrutinize committed (Simplify alone counts, whatever Scrutinize's STATUS is). Otherwise skip it. Its scope is changed-only over what the two agents changed:

Agent(subagent_type="Validate", run_in_background=false):
"FILES_CHANGED: {output of `git diff --name-only HEAD_BEFORE..HEAD`}
VALIDATION_SCOPE: changed-only
Run build, typecheck, lint, test on modified files"

**If FAIL:** Report validation failures to user and halt
**If PASS:** Continue to report

### Phase 4: Report

**Requires:** SCRUTINIZE_STATUS, VALIDATION_RESULT

Display summary:

## Self-Review Complete

**Files Reviewed**: {n}
**Status**: {PASS|FIXED|BLOCKED}

### Simplify agent
- {n} files refined for clarity

### Scrutinize agent (9-Pillar Evaluation)
| Pillar | Status |
|--------|--------|
| Design | {status} |
| Functionality | {status} |
| Security | {status} |
| Complexity | {status} |
| Error Handling | {status} |
| Tests | {status} |
| Naming | {status} |
| Consistency | {status} |
| Documentation | {status} |

### Commits Created
- {sha} {message}

{If BLOCKED: ### Blocking Issue\n{description}}

{{knowledge_writeback()}}

## Architecture

/self-review (orchestrator)
│
├─ Phase 0: Context gathering
│  ├─ Git diff for changed files
<!-- learning:on -->
│  ├─ Record HEAD_BEFORE
│  └─ Read index.md → DECISIONS_CONTEXT
<!-- learning:off -->
│  └─ Record HEAD_BEFORE
<!-- learning:end -->
│
├─ Phase 1: Simplify agent
│  └─ Code refinement (commits directly)
│
├─ Phase 2: Scrutinize agent
│  └─ 9-pillar quality gate (may fix and commit)
│
├─ Phase 3: Validate agent (conditional)
│  └─ If HEAD moved since HEAD_BEFORE (Simplify or Scrutinize committed), changed-only Validate over HEAD_BEFORE..HEAD
│
└─ Phase 4: Report
   └─ Display summary with pillar status

## Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|------|----------|
| No changes | Report "No changes to review" and exit |
| Simplify agent finds nothing | Normal, continue to Scrutinize agent |
| Scrutinize agent BLOCKED | Report blocking issue, halt workflow |
| Validation fails | Report failures, halt (don't create broken state) |
| Not in git repo | Report error, suggest running in git repo |

## Principles

1. **Orchestration only** - Command spawns agents, doesn't do the work
2. **Sequential execution** - Simplify agent must complete before Scrutinize agent
3. **Validation gate** - If Simplify agent or Scrutinize agent committed, the changes must pass validation
4. **Honest reporting** - Display actual agent outputs
5. **Fail fast** - Stop on BLOCKED or validation failure
